WEBVTT

00:27:29.003 --> 00:27:30.982
The no-eye-contact guy said,

00:27:31.006 --> 00:27:32.892
"This may look like a rotten apple,

00:27:32.916 --> 00:27:35.395
but it's actually an aged antique apple,

00:27:35.419 --> 00:27:38.576
and you could plant the apple seeds
in your backyard if you want."

00:27:38.899 --> 00:27:41.562
I hired him, and he ended up being
the best salesperson

00:27:41.586 --> 00:27:42.993
I ever worked with.

00:27:44.709 --> 00:27:48.355
That rotten-apple challenge
is what we'd call a work sample.

00:27:48.379 --> 00:27:50.552
A relevant piece of work
candidates have done,

00:27:50.576 --> 00:27:53.737
or one they do as part
of the application process.

00:27:54.067 --> 00:27:57.168
Work samples can be as simple
as they are powerful.

00:27:57.798 --> 00:28:00.950
They can showcase the candidates'
skills and values in real time,